Integrity ensures data is not altered or tampered with.

Availability ensures systems and data are accessible  
when needed.

---

## Hashing
Hashing is used to detect changes in data by producing  
a fixed-length output.

Even a small change in the input will completely  
change the hash.

It is commonly used in file verification, password  
storage, and integrity checks.

---

## Encryption and Decryption
Encryption converts readable data (plaintext) into  
unreadable data (ciphertext).

Decryption reverses this process to make the data  
readable again.

This protects sensitive information during transmission.

---

## Digital Signatures
Digital signatures use a hash and a private key to  
verify both integrity and authenticity.

They confirm that data has not been changed and that  
it came from a trusted source.

This is widely used in certificates and secure  
communications.

---

## Public Key Infrastructure (PKI)
PKI is a system that manages digital certificates  
and encryption keys.

It establishes trust between systems using  
certificate authorities.

PKI is what allows secure communication over  
the internet, especially in HTTPS.
